## Exact Cayley identity

Write the selected Cayley equation and correction direction as

```text
Phi = u K + v E + s F_B89,
K   = w^2-F6,
s C = s t0 C0.
```

Consequently

```text
partial_u Phi = K,
partial_t0(s C) = s C0,
partial_u(s C) = 0.
```

For every ternary degree-six monomial `m`, let

```text
N_m = (F6^2/16) m
```

in the 190-dimensional update component, and put

```text
y_m = (C0(F6+w^2)/16) m t2^3 s^2
```

in the `partial_u Phi` base block. Direct multiplication gives

```text
(w^2-F6) C0(F6+w^2)m + C0 F6^2 m = C0 w^4 m.
```

The complete target monomial basis shows that every monomial on the right is
outside the selected 24,767-row core. Therefore its core projection is zero:

```text
A_core y_m + U N_m = 0.
```

The correction direction has no `u` dependence. Every exact coefficient
matrix of `W` is accordingly zero on the 317 core coordinates used by the
lifts, and hence

```text
W y_m = 0.
```

Together these are the required characteristic-zero bordered syzygies.
Their six `Z[gamma]` coefficient residuals vanish entrywise. Each of the 28
lift columns is a monomial shift of the same 119-term numerator.

The `w^4` remainder is not claimed to vanish in the complete Macaulay space.
It lies in quotient rows and noncore singleton components. What matters for
the Schur coupling is the proved fact that it has no selected core row.

